From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: skip eDMA detection when its driver is unreachable

The DesignWare host probes eDMA registers and validates DMA interrupts even
when dw_edma_probe() is a stub returning -ENODEV. On IPQ4019 this reports
"Invalid eDMA IRQs found" despite CONFIG_DW_EDMA being disabled.

Use the same IS_REACHABLE condition as linux/dma/edma.h before probing the
optional DMA engine. Keep normal detection and IRQ validation when the
DMA driver is reachable; PCIe enumeration and endpoint DMA are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c
@@ -1128,6 +1128,10 @@
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	/* Match the availability of dw_edma_probe() in linux/dma/edma.h. */
+	if (!IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_DW_EDMA))
+		return 0;
+
 	/* Don't fail if no eDMA was found (for the backward compatibility) */
 	ret = dw_pcie_edma_find_chip(pci);
 	if (ret)
